  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Between 1995 and 1997 Robert Mosebach produced 172 very closely handwritten pages for a novel provisionally entitled Das Lamm (The Lamb), but published in 2000 as "Eine lange Nacht" (A Long Night). In 2002, Rebecca Horn staged the story of the long night for a photo shoot on location at the original sites in Frankfurt/Main. Twenty-four photo-paintings are based on this material. This artists' book draws all this material together: Martin Mosebach's manuscripts are reproduced as facsimiles on 200 pages with the photo-paintings inserted loose between the pages like bookmarks or notes.--Publisher's website (viewed on June 20, 2007).</subfield>
  </datafield>
